/*
 * Declares the CallOperatorValue class.
 *
 * CallOperatorValue is the abstract ancestor of all operator values involved in
 * invoking callable entities. This includes:
 *
 *   - direct function calls,
 *   - constructor calls,
 *   - method calls,
 *   - function-pointer calls,
 *   - and any other construct that produces a call frame.
 *
 * A call operator represents the semantic act of invoking something that can be
 * executed. It never produces an lvalue, and it is never considered a full
 * literal, since calls inherently depend on runtime evaluation.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::call
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/call.yr
 * @Author(s):
